      "committer": {
        "name": "_Kerman",
        "email": "kermanx@qq.com",
        "date": "2026-10-28T06:08:30Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(plugin-manager): stream the install diagnostics a failed run already holds\n\nA failed installation could show the generic sentence while its details\npanel stayed empty. A pnpm run that printed nothing had its diagnostic\nwritten to the complete log and the result but never streamed, and the\nGitHub connection check that stops an installation before pnpm ran kept\nits captured output only in the result. Both now reach the install-log\nstream the dialog renders: the no-output diagnostic streams as the run's\noutput, and a network or timeout check failure streams the exact\ngit ls-remote command line and its output as the installation's only\nrun under the caller's request id, with no exit code when the check\ntimed out. A check failure pnpm may resolve streams nothing.",
